new file mode 100644
index 0000000..00f5245
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/v6/source/EDGE_STORAGE_ORDER_PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# Native v6 edge storage permutation correction
+
+This additive patch concerns only v6 source-level native closed-loop probe semantics.
+It does not change the original NeuroMantle C transition core, declared molecular
+contacts, neuron labels, stimulation, 48-tick run length, or historic evidence.
+The release archive remains an immutable historical artifact.
+
+## Defect and scope
+
+The original feedback loop multiplied `net->edges[e].weight` by `e+1`, where
+`e` was a mutable physical array position. Permuting complete edge records
+before a trial changed the feedback target even if the graph, edge parameters,
+seed and external stimulation were identical. Fixed-feedback and frozen/STDP
+controls are important: this is a source-level feedback policy dependency,
+not evidence that the native SNN core is defective or that graph classification
+or biology can be inferred from one comparison.
+
+## Minimal correction
+
+A probe now records the authored edge identity in the order that `link(...)`
+created each complete native edge. After graph construction, the immutable edge
+attributes (`src`, `dst`, `delay`, `initial_weight`, `min_weight`, `max_weight`,
+`plus`, `minus`, `window`) establish a mapping from each authored ordinal to its
+current storage slot. At each tick the **original weighted feedback formula**
+uses that ordinal and the matching current weight, preserving STDP behavior.
+The core is untouched. Duplicate complete edge records are matched by their
+indistinguishable initial attributes; their native STDP updates are identical.
+
+This fixes *storage permutations after construction and before execution*.
+The code still treats the **authoring/creation order** as part of its defined
+feedback input. It is not a proof of generic graph-isomorphism invariance or
+of invariance under arbitrary reauthoring or mid-run edge mutation.
+Future graph-only experiments would need a newly declared representation or
+feedback policy and new trained/validated statistical results.
+
+## Tests and limits
+
+Compile normal and `-DNM_V6_TEST_REVERSE_EDGE_STORAGE` variants of
+`portable_kf1_ring.cpp` and `portable_newseeds.cpp` against the identical
+preserved v4 bridge and NeuroMantle C source. The macro reverses *complete*
+edge records immediately after graph construction. For direct inspection of
+feedback targets, also compile both variants with
+`-DNM_V6_TEST_TRACE_FEEDBACK`: this appends the 47 feedback targets as a test-only
+field and does not alter regular historical JSONL receipts.
+
+Run each with its original six-case catalog and `seed_count=256`. Check all
+records using `python3 research/v6/source/tests/check_edge_storage_invariance.py
+normal.jsonl reverse.jsonl [--historical historical.jsonl]` from the root
+of the extracted source tree. The normal, uninstrumented receipt must also
+match the appropriate archived 6,144 or 2,048 records exactly.
+
+Do not compare `final_sha256` between two physical edge permutations because
+`canonical_state` serializes edges in their current array order. The patched
+`base_weights` field is restored to its original 324 scaffold-edge meaning,
+but is still **not** a substitute for comparing neural behavior.
+
+The historical model scores, permutations and p-values are not recalculated by
+this source-only patch. It must not be represented as biological validation,
+new model accuracy, or an independent replication of the full study.
+
+## Distribution
+
+Apply this `.patch` to a *new extraction* of the archived
+`N-Molecular-v11-RESEARCH-20261023` tree, **not** to the immutable ZIP or the
+original published measurements. In a GitHub repository where this source
+is carried inside an LFS ZIP, the standalone patch may be uploaded as a small
+new tracked file without replacing the ZIP; users explicitly apply it to a
+working source extraction. Root `RELEASE_SHA256SUMS` describes unmodified
+release files, and will intentionally not validate edited source bytes.
+
+## Independent execution evidence for this source patch (2 November 2026)
+
+The historical archived source ZIP was validated as 110,759,586 bytes with
+SHA-256 `50a94cf97d29adfab846a83d264c4cf40596fa4cd46c7cc7846cb5d54405fbbc`
+and 1,267 CRC-valid members. Native baseline and patched normal-order replay
+matched all 6,144 fresh-seed and 2,048 ring-control JSONL bytes. Full reverse
+of all complete edge records yielded zero differences in the declared neural
+behavioral fields across those same 8,192 comparisons; additionally all 47
+feedback targets per trial matched in 2,048 ring trials using test-only trace
+instrumentation. The unpatched reverse actually reproduced the reported
+feedback-dependent failures (512/512 temporal differences in each closed-loop
+plasticity arm). A deliberate in-memory altered receipt was rejected.
+
+81 project-level Python tests passed after restoring executable permissions
+lost by ZIP extraction in an isolated working copy. The patched ring-control
+2,048 rows were identical when compiled by GCC and Clang. A native ASan+UBSan
+sample of 64 reversed-edge ring-control trials completed and exactly matched
+the unsanitized patched results. **The full upstream NeuroMantle `make test`
+was not a pass:** it reached `test_combined` (pass) then failed in
+`combined_integration.py` on a five-qubit QECC certificate refusal. The test
+was outside this source patch; this failure is retained, not waived.
+
+These checks were run against preserved Library archives, **not a verified
+checkout of the reported GitHub commit**. The original source ZIP remains
+unchanged. No full re-training, historical classifier re-permutation, or
+comprehensive upstream/sanitizer campaign is claimed by this patch.
